unit-redis-1.0.4 (1) keel; urgency=low

  * lib/redis.sh: a line of the comment redis_acl_fragment writes into
    /etc/redis/redis.conf.d/50-keel-secret.conf had lost its "#", so the
    first boot wrote a line Redis reads as a directive and redis-server
    refused to start ("Unresolved Configuration ... aborting"); found by the
    headless boot of the Redis 19.0-7 image. tests/redis.bats now checks that
    every line of the rendered fragment is a comment, a blank or a user rule,
    and starts a real redis-server on the shipped ACL file and the rendered
    fragment; the workflow installs redis-server for it.

